Volume = {24},
Number = {2},
Pages = {173-180},
Month = {AUG},
Abstract = {Hyperspectral remote sensing is opening new gateways for a multitude of
   applications with an added advantage of high spectral and spatial
   resolution. Target detection of urban objects has gained prominence
   during the past decade for maintaining a pace with increasing
   urbanization. This paper aims to identify roads and roofs as urban
   targets using a hybrid approach of the spectral and spatial aspect of
   hyperspectral data. The work highlights a brief taxonomy of
   morphological operators namely, Dilation, Erosion, Opening and Closing
   with fused spectral signatures of urban targets considered. Artificial
   neural network (ANN) has been used as a machine learning measure due to
   its high prediction capability and its effectiveness over conventional
   target detection approaches.
